Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:13:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-mini4: Enable the display pipe

iBoot leaves the iPad mini 4's 1536x2048 eDP panel running from its boot
framebuffer, the state the display pipe's driver adopts on the iPod
touch 6. Enable disp0 on both models (J96, J97), so that it replaces
simpledrm, with page flips and vblank interrupts and, once its self-check
of translated scanout passes, scanout of client buffers through the
display DART. dart-disp0 stays disabled: the driver enables it after
mapping the live scanout.

The panel mode is not in the ADT; the driver takes it from the boot
framebuffer. Its self-check needs one contiguous frame-sized buffer
(12 MiB here) from the 16 MiB CMA area, as on the iPad 5's panel of the
same size; if that allocation fails, the driver stays in bypass.

Not run on an iPad mini 4 yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
index d067921..e6f2e02 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
@@ -174,7 +174,9 @@
 /*
  * ADT displayport ("displayport,t7000", embedded, four lanes): the panel
  * link is eDP, so the pipe holds the dp domain instead of mipi_dsi and
- * gets the transmitter's window.
+ * gets the transmitter's window. The pipe takes the 1536x2048 panel over
+ * from simpledrm. No panel supply is given: the panel stays on in system
+ * sleep.
  */
 &disp0 {
 	reg = <0x2 0x06200000 0x0 0x100000>,
@@ -183,6 +185,7 @@
 	      <0x2 0x06700000 0x0 0x1000>;
 	reg-names = "adp", "dart0", "dart1", "dp";
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0>, <&ps_dp>;
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpu {
-- 
